BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edmonton Fringe Festival
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260824
DTSTAMP:20260809T022900Z
UID:ecdebf2693b87f1a6bf2e47bfd2254c5@explore-edmonton-calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/Fringe
 -photo-by-Marc-Chalifoux-DSC_0925_work.jpg
DESCRIPTION:North America’s biggest and oldest Fringe Festival!\n\nThe E
 dmonton International Fringe Theatre Festival is the largest and longest-r
 unning Fringe festival in North America - and one of the most celebrated i
 n the world. For 11 unforgettable days\, Fringe transforms Edmonton into a
  hub of theatre\, music\, magic\, comedy\, and community\, where anyone ca
 n be an Artist and everyone belongs!\n\nWith more than 200 indoor theatre 
 productions and over 1\,300 live performances\, there's no shortage of inc
 redible shows to discover. From storytelling and musical theatre to improv
 \, comedy\, and drama\, the festival showcases bold\, original work from l
 ocal\, national\, and international Artists.\n\nBeyond the stage\, visitor
 s can explore pêhonân\, a free gathering space where Indigenous Artists 
 from Treaty 6 Territory and the Métis homeland share stories\, workshops\
 , performances\, and cultural experiences at the Community of Tipis\, loca
 ted on the greenspace south of the Strathcona Community League.\n\nFamilie
 s won't want to miss KidsFringe\, a free program created especially for ch
 ildren 12 and under and their caregivers\, featuring performances\, worksh
 ops\, crafts\, and hands-on activities designed to spark creativity and fu
 n.\n\nMusic lovers can enjoy the free Fringe Music Series in ATB Park\, fe
 aturing an exciting lineup of local and touring talent\, while festival-go
 ers can also wander the grounds to discover captivating outdoor performers
 \, unique artisan vendors\, delicious food\, and family-friendly Fringe pa
 tios serving local brews.\n\nWhile Old Strathcona serves as the heart of t
 he festival\, Fringe extends well beyond the neighbourhood\, with performa
 nces taking place throughout Edmonton\, including the French Quarter\, 124
  Street\, Downtown\, and more!\n\nThis year\, guests are also invited to D
 iscover Fringe: A Very Important Fringer (VIF) Experience ! Enjoy a guided
  tour of the Festival Grounds\, hear behind-the-scenes stories\, take a ch
 ance on a surprise show in your chosen genre\, and connect with expert Fri
 ngers over a drink. Your ticket also includes a 2026 Festival Guide\, a co
 py of The Fringers' Almanac \, and insider tips from knowledgeable volunte
 ers to help you make the most of your Fringe adventure. By the end of the 
 experience\, you'll know your way around\, have discovered something new\,
  and be ready to plan what to see next!\n\nEVENT INFORMATION\nLocation: Ol
 d Strathcona and Whyte Avenue\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA\nVisit / Tickets: 
 https://www.fringetheatre.ca/festival/\nExplore Edmonton: https://exploree
 dmonton.com/event-calendar/edmonton-fringe-festival
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T022832Z
LOCATION:Old Strathcona and Whyte Avenue\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/edmonton-fringe-festival
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>North America’s biggest and oldest Fring
 e Festival!</p><p>The Edmonton International Fringe Theatre Festival is th
 e largest and longest-running Fringe festival in North America - and one o
 f the most celebrated in the world. For 11 unforgettable days\, Fringe tra
 nsforms Edmonton into a hub of theatre\, music\, magic\, comedy\, and comm
 unity\, where anyone can be an Artist and everyone belongs!</p><p>With mor
 e than 200 indoor theatre productions and over 1\,300 live performances\, 
 there&#x27\;s no shortage of incredible shows to discover. From storytelli
 ng and musical theatre to improv\, comedy\, and drama\, the festival showc
 ases bold\, original work from local\, national\, and international Artist
 s.</p><p>Beyond the stage\, visitors can explore pêhonân\, a free gather
 ing space where Indigenous Artists from Treaty 6 Territory and the Métis 
 homeland share stories\, workshops\, performances\, and cultural experienc
 es at the Community of Tipis\, located on the greenspace south of the Stra
 thcona Community League.</p><p>Families won&#x27\;t want to miss KidsFring
 e\, a free program created especially for children 12 and under and their 
 caregivers\, featuring performances\, workshops\, crafts\, and hands-on ac
 tivities designed to spark creativity and fun.</p><p>Music lovers can enjo
 y the free Fringe Music Series in ATB Park\, featuring an exciting lineup 
 of local and touring talent\, while festival-goers can also wander the gro
 unds to discover captivating outdoor performers\, unique artisan vendors\,
  delicious food\, and family-friendly Fringe patios serving local brews.</
 p><p>While Old Strathcona serves as the heart of the festival\, Fringe ext
 ends well beyond the neighbourhood\, with performances taking place throug
 hout Edmonton\, including the French Quarter\, 124 Street\, Downtown\, and
  more!</p><p>This year\, guests are also invited to Discover Fringe: A Ver
 y Important Fringer (VIF) Experience ! Enjoy a guided tour of the Festival
  Grounds\, hear behind-the-scenes stories\, take a chance on a surprise sh
 ow in your chosen genre\, and connect with expert Fringers over a drink. Y
 our ticket also includes a 2026 Festival Guide\, a copy of The Fringers&#x
 27\; Almanac \, and insider tips from knowledgeable volunteers to help you
  make the most of your Fringe adventure. By the end of the experience\, yo
 u&#x27\;ll know your way around\, have discovered something new\, and be r
 eady to plan what to see next!</p><h3>Event Information</h3><ul><li><stron
 g>Location:</strong> Old Strathcona and Whyte Avenue\, Edmonton\, Alberta\
 , CA</li><li><strong>Visit / Tickets:</strong> https://www.fringetheatre.c
 a/festival/</li><li><strong>Explore Edmonton:</strong> https://exploreedmo
 nton.com/event-calendar/edmonton-fringe-festival</li></ul>
