 g_3-large.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Edmonton’s on par for excitement as the LPGA Tour rolls in f
 or 2026!\n\nGet ready\, Edmonton! The LPGA Tour’s brightest stars are co
 ming to Edmonton as Royal Mayfair Golf Club hosts the 2026 CPKC Women’s 
 Open\, Canada’s National Women’s Open Championship. Taking place Augus
 t 17–23\, 2026\, this will be the 52nd playing of the championship and t
 he third time Royal Mayfair has welcomed the event. Past champions here in
 clude LPGA Tour legend Lorena Ochoa and Lydia Ko\, who captured the title 
 in 2013 at just 15 years old! More than just a tournament\, the CPKC Women
 ’s Open is one of Canada’s top sporting events and a must-watch stop o
 n the LPGA Tour. Fans can expect thrilling competition\, electric crowds\,
  and a chance to be part of something bigger. Thanks to the CPKC Has Heart
  program\, the event has raised over $23 million for pediatric heart healt
 h across Canada since 2014. Stay tuned for details on tickets\, volunteer 
 spots\, and hospitality packages.\n\nEVENT INFORMATION\nLocation: Royal Ma
 yfair Golf Club - 9450 Groat Rd\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA\nVisit / Tickets
 : https://www.cpkcwomensopen.com/2025/07/16/edmontons-royal-mayfair-golf-c
 lub-to-host-2026-cpkc-womens-open/\nExplore Edmonton: https://exploreedmon
 ton.com/event-calendar/2026-cpkc-womens-open
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T022815Z
LOCATION:Royal Mayfair Golf Club - 9450 Groat Rd\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/2026-cpkc-womens-open
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>Edmonton’s on par for excitement as the 
 LPGA Tour rolls in for 2026!</p><p>Get ready\, Edmonton! The LPGA Tour’s
  brightest stars are coming to Edmonton as Royal Mayfair Golf Club hosts t
 he 2026 CPKC Women’s Open\, Canada’s National Women’s Open Champions
 hip. Taking place August 17–23\, 2026\, this will be the 52nd playing of
  the championship and the third time Royal Mayfair has welcomed the event.
  Past champions here include LPGA Tour legend Lorena Ochoa and Lydia Ko\, 
 who captured the title in 2013 at just 15 years old! More than just a tour
 nament\, the CPKC Women’s Open is one of Canada’s top sporting events 
 and a must-watch stop on the LPGA Tour. Fans can expect thrilling competit
 ion\, electric crowds\, and a chance to be part of something bigger. Thank
 s to the CPKC Has Heart program\, the event has raised over $23 million fo
