DESCRIPTION:A conversation about the RAM's newest featured exhibition.\n\n
 Death and dying can be difficult to talk about\, but the ways we commemora
 te those we have lost are among the most personal and meaningful expressio
 ns of our humanity.\n\nThis August\, the Royal Alberta Museum welcomes Eve
 rgreen Memorial’s Family Service Directors Samantha Berard and Rebekah D
 avid for In Conversation: How Do You Want To Be Remembered\, inspired by D
 eath: Life’s Greatest Mystery .\n\nThis intimate conversation will inclu
 de a short presentation\, an open Q&A with Berard and David\, and group di
 scussions with other attendees to explore end-of-life’s big questions an
 d reflect on how remembrance can foster connection and healing.\n\nTo ensu
 re a comfortable experience\, space is limited. Tickets are $36 and includ
 e General Admission into the RAM.\n\nEVENT INFORMATION\nLocation: Royal Al
 berta Museum - 9810 103a Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA\nVisit / Tickets: h
 ttps://atms.alberta.ca/ram/selection.aspx?sch=199486&_gl=1*6v1569*_gcl_aw*
