BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Edmonton Terry Fox Run
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
DTSTAMP:20260809T022900Z
UID:bc7aa6de37b561d7d15760881a797268@explore-edmonton-calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/Edmont
 on_Summer_Skyline_Walterdale_Bridge_Ariel_North_Saskatchewan_River.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Learn more about Terry Fox's remarkable legacy.\n\nThe story o
 f the Canadian\, Terry Fox\, is known very well across the nation.\n\nA yo
 ung man from Coquitlam\, BC awed the nation in 1980 with an ambitious goal
  to raise $1 from every Canadian for cancer research\, by running from coa
 st to coast across the country. Word about his goal spread and news outlet
 s began to cover the race across the nation as people lined up highways\, 
 and communities greeted Terry as he moved his way from town to town. He ma
 de it an astonishing 5\,373 kilometres before cancer returned to his lungs
 \, forcing him to stop his race. To continue the legacy\, Canada unites to
  keep the run going\, running the Terry Fox Run every September.\n\nAttend
  this free event in the beautiful Kinsmen Park located between the Walterd
 ale and High-Level bridges. Run the full 10km route or stop when you want 
 to - you decide how long you run. Registration is free\, all are welcome\,
  and the event is noncompetitive. You are also invited to register a team 
 and help fundraise for cancer research at https://run.terryfox.ca/edmonton
  .\n\nJoin a meaningful event that has been a symbol of Canadian connected
 ness and a hopeful example of how one person can make a difference.\n\nEVE
 NT INFORMATION\nLocation: Kinsmen Park - 9100 Walterdale Hill\, Edmonton\,
  AB\, CA\nVisit / Tickets: https://run.terryfox.ca/129794\nExplore Edmonto
 n: https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/edmonton-terry-fox-run-2026
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T022833Z
LOCATION:Kinsmen Park - 9100 Walterdale Hill\, Edmonton\, AB\, CA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/edmonton-terry-fox-run-2026
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>Learn more about Terry Fox&#x27\;s remarka
 ble legacy.</p><p>The story of the Canadian\, Terry Fox\, is known very we
 ll across the nation.</p><p>A young man from Coquitlam\, BC awed the natio
 n in 1980 with an ambitious goal to raise $1 from every Canadian for cance
 r research\, by running from coast to coast across the country. Word about
  his goal spread and news outlets began to cover the race across the natio
 n as people lined up highways\, and communities greeted Terry as he moved 
 his way from town to town. He made it an astonishing 5\,373 kilometres bef
 ore cancer returned to his lungs\, forcing him to stop his race. To contin
 ue the legacy\, Canada unites to keep the run going\, running the Terry Fo
 x Run every September.</p><p>Attend this free event in the beautiful Kinsm
 en Park located between the Walterdale and High-Level bridges. Run the ful
 l 10km route or stop when you want to - you decide how long you run. Regis
 tration is free\, all are welcome\, and the event is noncompetitive. You a
 re also invited to register a team and help fundraise for cancer research 
 at https://run.terryfox.ca/edmonton .</p><p>Join a meaningful event that h
 as been a symbol of Canadian connectedness and a hopeful example of how on
 e person can make a difference.</p><h3>Event Information</h3><ul><li><stro
 ng>Location:</strong> Kinsmen Park - 9100 Walterdale Hill\, Edmonton\, AB\
 , CA</li><li><strong>Visit / Tickets:</strong> https://run.terryfox.ca/129
 794</li><li><strong>Explore Edmonton:</strong> https://exploreedmonton.com
 /event-calendar/edmonton-terry-fox-run-2026</li></ul>
X-IMAGE:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/Edmonton_Summer_Skyline_
 Walterdale_Bridge_Ariel_North_Saskatchewan_River.jpg
X-TICKETS-URL:https://run.terryfox.ca/129794
END:VEVENT
