BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Story Of Linda Ronstadt
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261005
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261006
DTSTAMP:20260809T022900Z
UID:ec9046d093b13f45eaecfc15b229e048@explore-edmonton-calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/Jubile
 e-114.JPG
DESCRIPTION:A must-see performance this fall!\n\nLinda Ronstadt didn’t j
 ust make music - she made history. With smash hits like “You’re No Goo
 d\,” “Blue Bayou\,” and “When Will I Be Loved\,” she became one 
 of the best-selling artists of all time. They called her the Queen of Rock
 . But that title barely scratches the surface.\n\nHer story is one of push
 ing boundaries\, doing things her own way\, and making music that moved mi
 llions. It’s also a story of extraordinary courage - because when Parkin
 son’s disease threatened to silence the voice the world loved\, Ronstadt
  faced it head-on.\n\nIn The Story of Linda Ronstadt\, Country Music Alber
 ta’s Artist of The Year\, Mariya Stokes brings that voice back to life -
  raw\, powerful\, and completely authentic. Backed by a full live band\, M
 ariya takes you inside Ronstadt’s world through her greatest hits and th
 e engaging\, untold stories behind them. And it all unfolds against a stun
 ning multimedia presentation on a huge screen that puts you right in the h
 eart of the journey!\n\nEVENT INFORMATION\nLocation: Northern Alberta Jubi
 lee Auditorium - 11455 87 Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA\nExplore Edmonton:
  https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/the-story-of-linda-ronstadt
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T022856Z
LOCATION:Northern Alberta Jubilee Auditorium - 11455 87 Ave\, Edmonton\, A
 lberta\, CA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/the-story-of-linda-ronstadt
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>A must-see performance this fall!</p><p>Li
 nda Ronstadt didn’t just make music - she made history. With smash hits 
 like “You’re No Good\,” “Blue Bayou\,” and “When Will I Be Lov
 ed\,” she became one of the best-selling artists of all time. They calle
 d her the Queen of Rock. But that title barely scratches the surface.</p><
 p>Her story is one of pushing boundaries\, doing things her own way\, and 
 making music that moved millions. It’s also a story of extraordinary cou
 rage - because when Parkinson’s disease threatened to silence the voice 
 the world loved\, Ronstadt faced it head-on.</p><p>In The Story of Linda R
 onstadt\, Country Music Alberta’s Artist of The Year\, Mariya Stokes bri
 ngs that voice back to life - raw\, powerful\, and completely authentic. B
 acked by a full live band\, Mariya takes you inside Ronstadt’s world thr
 ough her greatest hits and the engaging\, untold stories behind them. And 
 it all unfolds against a stunning multimedia presentation on a huge screen
  that puts you right in the heart of the journey!</p><h3>Event Information
 </h3><ul><li><strong>Location:</strong> Northern Alberta Jubilee Auditoriu
 m - 11455 87 Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA</li><li><strong>Explore Edmonto
 n:</strong> https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/the-story-of-linda-
 ronstadt</li></ul>
X-IMAGE:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/Jubilee-114.JPG
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cinch Canadian Country Expo
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261006
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261012
DTSTAMP:20260809T022900Z
UID:1057febbad3e90477a47828d2a0fe14c@explore-edmonton-calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/Octobe
 r-4-CCE-Callie-100.jpg
DESCRIPTION:A can’t-miss experience for Western enthusiasts!\n\nThe Cinc
 h Canadian Country Expo takes over the Edmonton EXPO Centre this October\,
  bringing six days packed with shopping\, competition\, culture\, and West
 ern lifestyle\, all with free admission!\n\nAs the daytime heart of Canadi
 an Finals Rodeo (CFR) Week\, the Expo is where the Western spirit comes al
 ive beyond the arena. Explore 100+ premium vendors across a massive trades
 how floor featuring Western fashion\, home décor\, equipment\, lifestyle 
 brands\, and agricultural innovation. It is the place to shop\, connect\, 
 and experience the best of the Western community.\n\nBeyond the shopping\,
  the action is nonstop! Live arenas feature team roping\, barrel racing\, 
 the Canadian Youth Rodeo Championship (CYRC) presented by Saskatchewan Min
 ing & Minerals\, and bullfighting. Visitors can also take in educational c
 linics\, horsemanship workshops\, and heritage exhibits that celebrate bot
 h rodeo tradition and its future.\n\nFamilies are encouraged to join in th
 e fun with youth competitions\, hands-on activities\, interactive programm
 ing\, themed fashion days\, and lively fan activations happening all week 
 long!\n\nEVENT INFORMATION\nLocation: Edmonton EXPO Centre - 7515 118 Ave\
 , Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA\nVisit / Tickets: https://www.cfr.ca/CCE/home-ca
 nadian-county-expo\nExplore Edmonton: https://exploreedmonton.com/event-ca
 lendar/cinch-canadian-country-expo
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T022826Z
LOCATION:Edmonton EXPO Centre - 7515 118 Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/cinch-canadian-country-expo
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>A can’t-miss experience for Western enth
 usiasts!</p><p>The Cinch Canadian Country Expo takes over the Edmonton EXP
 O Centre this October\, bringing six days packed with shopping\, competiti
 on\, culture\, and Western lifestyle\, all with free admission!</p><p>As t
 he daytime heart of Canadian Finals Rodeo (CFR) Week\, the Expo is where t
 he Western spirit comes alive beyond the arena. Explore 100+ premium vendo
 rs across a massive tradeshow floor featuring Western fashion\, home déco
 r\, equipment\, lifestyle brands\, and agricultural innovation. It is the 
 place to shop\, connect\, and experience the best of the Western community
 .</p><p>Beyond the shopping\, the action is nonstop! Live arenas feature t
 eam roping\, barrel racing\, the Canadian Youth Rodeo Championship (CYRC) 
 presented by Saskatchewan Mining &amp\; Minerals\, and bullfighting. Visit
 ors can also take in educational clinics\, horsemanship workshops\, and he
 ritage exhibits that celebrate both rodeo tradition and its future.</p><p>
 Families are encouraged to join in the fun with youth competitions\, hands
 -on activities\, interactive programming\, themed fashion days\, and livel
 y fan activations happening all week long!</p><h3>Event Information</h3><u
 l><li><strong>Location:</strong> Edmonton EXPO Centre - 7515 118 Ave\, Edm
 onton\, Alberta\, CA</li><li><strong>Visit / Tickets:</strong> https://www
 .cfr.ca/CCE/home-canadian-county-expo</li><li><strong>Explore Edmonton:</s
 trong> https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/cinch-canadian-country-e
 xpo</li></ul>
