 fall!</p><p>A genuine renaissance man of roots music\, Colin Linden is a G
 rammy-winning guitarist\, singer\, songwriter\, and producer whose soulful
  blend of blues\, folk\, and Americana has taken him from Toronto coffeeho
 uses to Nashville’s biggest stages. He has also played on more than 500 
 albums and produced over 140\, working with legends like Bruce Cockburn\, 
 Bob Dylan\, Keb’ Mo’\, and Lucinda Williams!</p><p>Onstage at New Moon
  Folk Club\, expect masterful guitar work\, gritty vocals\, and stories fr
 om a lifetime in music\, in an intimate concert that feels like sitting in
  the studio with one of roots music’s true heavyweights.</p><p>Your guid
 e to celebrating National Indigenous History Month in Edmonton</p><h3>Even
 t Information</h3><ul><li><strong>Location:</strong> New Moon Folk Club - 
