ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/IIHF-W
 orld-Junior-Championship-Canada-vs-Finland-Gold_12-large-1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Where hockey history is made!\n\nThe IIHF World Junior Champio
 nship returns to Edmonton this winter\, bringing the world’s top under-2
 0 hockey players to Rogers Place in the heart of downtown’s ICE District
 .\n\nOne of hockey’s most celebrated international tournaments\, the Wor
 ld Juniors will see 10 national teams compete for gold. Rogers Place will 
 serve as the primary competition venue\, hosting 17 games (including the s
 emifinals and medal games!) while additional matchups will take place in R
 ed Deer.\n\nCo-hosted by Edmonton and Red Deer\, the 2027 IIHF World Junio
 r Championship continues Alberta’s proud tradition of hosting world-clas
 s hockey events and welcoming fans from around the globe!\n\nEVENT INFORMA
 TION\nSchedule: Dec 26\, 2026\, Jan 5\, 2027\nLocation: Rogers Place - 102
 20 104 Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA\nExplore Edmonton: https://exploreedm
 onton.com/event-calendar/2027-iihf-world-junior-championship
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T022817Z
LOCATION:Rogers Place - 10220 104 Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
