BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Story of Merle Haggard
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270121
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270122
DTSTAMP:20260809T022900Z
UID:4c1811ad21ac3a4de2afc175b9f9fb2a@explore-edmonton-calendar
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://assets.exploreedmonton.com/images/Jubile
 e-114.JPG
DESCRIPTION:A must-see show!\n\nBe part of a special evening dedicated to 
 one of the greatest artists in country music history - Merle Haggard. In 
 “The Story of Merle Haggard”\, JUNO-nominated singer Jess Lee takes gu
 ests on a journey through Haggard’s incredible life through stories and 
 songs. With a career spanning six decades\, Haggard rose from poverty and 
 prison to international fame through his songs about outlaws\, underdogs\,
  the heartbroken and the hard-living. He notched 40 No. 1 hits including "
 Working Man Blues”\, "Mama Tried”\, “Silver Wings” and one of the 
 most famous country songs of all time\, “Okie From Muskogee”.\n\nJess 
 Lee rose to fame as the lead singer of the Midnite Rodeo Band\, charting 1
 4 singles and numerous awards in the '80's before Lee went solo with songs
  like "Crowhill Road". Praised by Country Music News as the best pure coun
 try voice in Canada\, Lee effortlessly emulates the rich\, smooth baritone
  of Merle Haggard.\n\nEVENT INFORMATION\nLocation: Northern Alberta Jubile
 e Auditorium - 11455 87 Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA\nExplore Edmonton: h
 ttps://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/the-story-of-merle-haggard
LAST-MODIFIED:20260809T022856Z
LOCATION:Northern Alberta Jubilee Auditorium - 11455 87 Ave\, Edmonton\, A
 lberta\, CA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://exploreedmonton.com/event-calendar/the-story-of-merle-haggard
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>A must-see show!</p><p>Be part of a specia
 l evening dedicated to one of the greatest artists in country music histor
 y - Merle Haggard. In “The Story of Merle Haggard”\, JUNO-nominated si
 nger Jess Lee takes guests on a journey through Haggard’s incredible lif
 e through stories and songs. With a career spanning six decades\, Haggard 
 rose from poverty and prison to international fame through his songs about
  outlaws\, underdogs\, the heartbroken and the hard-living. He notched 40 
 No. 1 hits including &quot\;Working Man Blues”\, &quot\;Mama Tried”\, 
 “Silver Wings” and one of the most famous country songs of all time\, 
 “Okie From Muskogee”.</p><p>Jess Lee rose to fame as the lead singer o
 f the Midnite Rodeo Band\, charting 14 singles and numerous awards in the 
 &#x27\;80&#x27\;s before Lee went solo with songs like &quot\;Crowhill Roa
 d&quot\;. Praised by Country Music News as the best pure country voice in 
 Canada\, Lee effortlessly emulates the rich\, smooth baritone of Merle Hag
 gard.</p><h3>Event Information</h3><ul><li><strong>Location:</strong> Nort
 hern Alberta Jubilee Auditorium - 11455 87 Ave\, Edmonton\, Alberta\, CA</
